---
/**
 * The layered key visual, rebuilt from the Figma exports.
 *
 * Sits behind the poster content only — the logo footer lives below it, on the
 * flat canvas, exactly as in the Figma layouts.
 *
 * On the 944x1437 portrait artboard the export gives:
 *   glow rect  944x1437, radius 43.18 (4.57%), blurred sigma 38.86 (4.12%)
 *   sharp rect inset 90/69 -> 765x1298, square corners, canvas-colored
 *   pills      centred, canvas-colored, each with a larger blurred glow behind
 *
 * Both sharp shapes are filled with the canvas color; they only read because
 * of the blurred duplicates behind them.
 *
 * Placement comes from --kv-top / --kv-bottom / --kv-x (see global.css), which
 * pages override; the wide layouts also push the shapes past the text column,
 * as the landscape cover does.
 *
 * Color vars (--canvas / --glow) are inherited from #poster-bg on the wrap.
 */
---

{/* Sized container: the aspect query that picks portrait vs landscape reads
    off this element, so the shapes inside can react to it. */}
<div class="kv-area pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-0" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="kv-shapes absolute inset-0">
    {/* Bleeds past the frame on every side — this is the halo, and its blur
        keeps the edge soft where the wrap clips it. */}
    <div class="kv-glow absolute rounded-[4%/3%] bg-[var(--glow)] blur-[var(--kv-blur)]">
    </div>

    {/* Sharp rectangle, and the size container the pills measure themselves
        against: a wide frame lays the pill down, as in the cover layout. */}
    <div class="kv-frame absolute flex items-center justify-center bg-[var(--canvas)]">
      <div class="kv-pill kv-pill--glow bg-[var(--glow)] blur-[var(--kv-blur)]"></div>
      <div class="kv-pill kv-pill--sharp bg-[var(--canvas)]"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
